{
  "an4.173:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 4.173 ",
  "an4.173:0.2": "18. Intention ",
  "an4.173:0.3": "With Mahākoṭṭhita ",
  "an4.173:1.1": "Then Venerable Mahākoṭṭhita went up to Venerable Sāriputta, and exchanged greetings with him. ",
  "an4.173:1.2": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, Mahākoṭṭhita sat down to one side, and said to Sāriputta: ",
  "an4.173:2.1": "“Reverend, when the six fields of contact have faded away and ceased with no residue left behind, does something else still exist?” ",
  "an4.173:3.1": "“Don’t put it like that, reverend.” ",
  "an4.173:4.1": "“Does something else no longer exist?” ",
  "an4.173:5.1": "“Don’t put it like that, reverend.” ",
  "an4.173:6.1": "“Does something else both still exist and no longer exist?” ",
  "an4.173:7.1": "“Don’t put it like that, reverend.” ",
  "an4.173:8.1": "“Does something else neither still exist nor no longer exist?” ",
  "an4.173:9.1": "“Don’t put it like that, reverend.” ",
  "an4.173:10.1": "“Reverend, when asked whether—when the six fields of contact have faded away and ceased with no residue left behind—something else still exists, you say ‘don’t put it like that’. ",
  "an4.173:10.2": "When asked whether something else no longer exists, ",
  "an4.173:10.3": "you say ‘don’t put it like that’. ",
  "an4.173:10.4": "When asked whether something else both still exists and no longer exists, ",
  "an4.173:10.5": "you say ‘don’t put it like that’